<title>SWEDEN: SECURITAS FALL ON LOWER GROWTH FORECAST.</title>
<headline>SECURITAS FALL ON LOWER GROWTH FORECAST.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish security company Securitas dropped on Wednesday after it posted a largely unchanged profit for the first six months of 1997 of 230 million crowns against 228 million a year ago.</p>
<p>At 1200 GMT the share was 11 crowns lower at 210. It had been trading three crowns down ahead of the report.</p>
<p>&quot;The result was lower than expectations and the company also lowered its growth forecast to 10-15 percent having previously forecast longterm growth of 20 percent,&quot; said a Stockholm based analyst.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
